{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#511","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#511","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#511\",\"parent_revision\":\"7b209861ca8d065b478e2ab82fabc42c0a1d044e4b3238f0b62863d1e8dd2ac9\",\"root_revision\":\"7b209861ca8d065b478e2ab82fabc42c0a1d044e4b3238f0b62863d1e8dd2ac9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nbacklog_sync and backlog_pull block the MCP client for the duration of all GitHub API calls (one per item). FastMCP v3 supports task=True on @mcp.tool which executes the tool as a background task \u2014 the client receives a task handle immediately and can poll status. Combined with ctx.report_progress(i, total), clients get a progress bar during batch operations.\\n\\nFiles affected: .claude/skills/backlog/backlog_core/server.py, pyproject.toml (add fastmcp[tasks] extra)\\n\\nChanges required:\\n1. Add fastmcp[tasks] to optional dependencies in pyproject.toml\\n2. Change @mcp.tool() to @mcp.tool(task=True) on backlog_sync and backlog_pull\\n3. Add Progress dependency injection and emit ctx.report_progress(i, total) at each item iteration\\n\\nSource: fastmcp v3 docs servers/tasks.mdx \u2014 task=True + Progress injection for background tools\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | FastMCP v3 task=True pattern | AVAILABLE | Item description cites fastmcp v3 docs |\\n| 2 | Duplicate of #469 | AVAILABLE | Both items describe identical change to same files |\\n\\nVerdict: DUPLICATE \u2014 this item is functionally identical to #469. Recommend closing this one (#511) as a duplicate of #469, or merging into #469.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Duplicate of #469. Should be closed.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `backlog_sync` and `backlog_pull` use `@mcp.tool(task=True)` for background execution\\n- `fastmcp[tasks]` extra added to pyproject.toml dependencies\\n- `ctx.report_progress(i, total)` called per item during iteration\\n- Callers receive a task ID immediately and can poll for completion\\n- Regression: tool behavior and outputs unchanged\\n- Note: this item overlaps significantly with #469 ('Add background task support to backlog_sync and backlog_pull via task=True') which may be the same feature.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 (see #469)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` \u2014 (see #469)\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a caller of `backlog_sync` and `backlog_pull` on a large backlog, I need these operations to execute as background tasks with progress reporting so the MCP connection does not block during 10-30 second batch operations.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **backlog_sync and backlog_pull: add task=true background execution with ctx.report_progress()** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: fastmcp-creator skill analysis of backlog_core/server.py\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"53daf2d3282c26b12329cce7c5c689ea81b5c34a7a1b3b322e9517b867b41e01\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTCqUg\"}"}